\par He shook his head in puzzlement.  "Emma, I have no idea what you mean.  What's happened?"
\par 
\par "I hope you're telling the truth, Axen, but it makes no difference in the outcome of our talks today.  As of now, they're over."
\par 
\par She glanced back as two uniformed men dragged a third man into camera range.  The man's wrists were cuffed behind him, and the guards stood on either side holding him up.  A large bruise stained one side of his face.
\par 
